  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Retrieve information about the transitions of a state\nIt was previously impossible to retrieve informations about the transitions of a state once they were created.\nNow, the IState<T> interface exposes some methods that allows to retrieve the transitions of a state.\n\n- `GetTransitions()` returns all the tokens that can trigger transitions.\n- `GetTransition(token)` returns the transition triggered for a token\n- `GetTransitionsCount` returns the number of transitions defined for the state.\n\nMoreover, the `ClearTranstitions()` method allows to clear all the transitions of a state, except for the default transition.\n\n# More documentation\nThere is a whole section in the documentation about states.\nThis section describes `evolutive states`, that are states for which transitions cannot be defined before the state is reached.\nFor example, the number of transitions may vary depending on previous inputs, so `evolutive states` try to answer this problem.\n\nMore information is available in the [documentation about states](Doc/States.md).",
